{"answerArea":{"calculator":true,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"###The strategy\n\nLet's rewrite $3^{x}$ as an expression whose exponent is $5x$, by using the exponential property $k^{b \\cdot c} = (k^b)^{c}$. \n\n\nThen,  the base of this rewritten expression would be equal to $A$. ","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"###Rewriting $3^{x}$\n\n\n$\\begin{align} 3^{x} \u0026= 3\\^{\\Large \\frac15\\ \\cdot \\ 5x} \u0026\u0026\u0026\u0026 \\normalsize\\text{since } x=\\dfrac{5x}{5}\\\\\\\\\n \u0026= (3\\^{\\large \\frac15})^{5x}  \u0026\u0026\u0026\u0026 \\normalsize \\text{since }k^{b \\cdot c} = (k^b)^{c}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"###Finding the value of $A$\n\nWe have rewritten $3^{x}$ as $(\\blueD{3\\^{\\large \\frac15}})^{5x }$. \n\n**So it follows that $\\blueD A = \\blueD{3\\^{\\large \\frac15}}$**.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**What is the value of $A$ when we rewrite $3^{x}$ as  $A^{5x}$** ?\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$A=3\\^{\\large \\frac15}$","correct":true},{"content":"$A=3^{}$","correct":false},{"content":"$A=3^{- 5}$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"$A=3\\^{\\Large -\\large \\frac15}$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"countChoices":false,"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"randomize":true},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
